       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "title": "Midnight Snacks",
   "goal": "Present bias",
   "target_s": 25,
   "shots": [
    {
     "sequence": {
      "type": "narration",
      "settings": [
       "grocery"
      ],
      "mood": "funny",
      "seed": 6,
      "actors": [
       {
        "k": "maya",
        "x": 960
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       "At one in the morning, Maya walks to the all night shop for focus snacks.",
       "She stands in the aisle comparing three kinds of crackers for ten minutes.",
       "Tomorrow morning feels like someone else's problem, a stranger she barely knows.",
       "Some studies suggest we think about our future self almost like a stranger.",
       "That finding is still debated, but it fits the aisle perfectly."
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "title": "Two In The Morning",
   "goal": "Cost",
   "target_s": 25,
   "shots": [
    {
     "sequence": {
      "type": "narration",
      "settings": [
       "desk_room"
      ],
      "mood": "tense",
      "seed": 7,
      "actors": [
       {
        "k": "maya",
        "x": 960
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       "At two, Maya finally opens the file again. The slide is still blank.",
       "Now the tightness has company: panic, with its loud little drum.",
       "She has seven hours, and she has already spent most of them.",
       "Every hour she avoided cost her an hour of sleep and some calm.",
       "The task has not grown. Only the pressure around it has."
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "title": "What Is It Really",
   "goal": "Dawn truth",
   "target_s": 25,
   "shots": [
    {
     "sequence": {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "setting": "dawn_kitchen",
      "mood": "warm",
      "seed": 8,
      "a": {
       "k": "maya",
       "x": 560
      },
      "b": {
       "k": "theo",
       "x": 1360
      },
      "lines": [
       {
        "who": "theo",
        "t": "You look awful. Tea? What is actually scary about this talk?"
       },
       {
        "who": "maya",
        "t": "Nothing. Everything. I think my first slide will be bad."
       },
       {
        "who": "theo",
        "t": "So write a bad first slide. Nobody has to see it."
       },
       {
        "who": "maya",
        "t": "A bad slide. I can do a bad slide in two minutes."
       },
       {
        "who": "theo",
        "t": "Then do it, and I will keep the kettle going."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "title": "A Rough Draft",
   "goal": "The payoff and honest cost",
   "target_s": 25,
   "shots": [
    {
     "sequence": {
      "type": "narration",
      "settings": [
       "kitchen_morning"
      ],
      "mood": "warm",
      "seed": 9,
      "actors": [
       {
        "k": "maya",
        "x": 960
       }
      ],
      "cues": [
       "The bad first slide takes four minutes. The second takes three.",
       "By six, there is a rough deck, ugly fonts and all.",
       "It is not brilliant. She slept two hours and it shows.",
       "But the feeling that kept her away shrank once she was inside the work.",
       "Starting turned out to be the smallest part of the job."
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
